      "B": {
        "reading_checked": "If the chart title is an authoritative statement of the City A population trend for 2010-2015 and the workflow maps a stated shrinking trend to decline response, select the decline-response route.",
        "evidence": "The condition requires the title to be an 'authoritative statement' of the trend. The visual evidence (the plotted line rising from 2,000 to 3,000) directly contradicts the title's assertion of a 'shrinking' population. Without an explicit policy stating that the title overrides the plotted data, the condition that the title is the authoritative statement of the trend is not met.",
        "status": "refuted"
      }
    },
    "r2": {
      "O": {
        "1": {
          "evidence": "The title contains 'Shrinking Population', and the blue line's endpoint at 2015 (approx 3,000) is higher on the page than its endpoint at 2010 (approx 2,000).",
          "status": "supported"
        }
      },
      "B": {
        "reading_checked": "If contradictory chart signals cannot be resolved and no supplied policy specifies a route for conflicting or insufficient evidence, routine monitoring is a possible conservative route only if the workflow permits it for unresolved trends.",
        "evidence": "The condition requires a 'workflow rule allowing routine monitoring for unresolved evidence'. The provided task instructions and form fields do not contain any such rule. The instructions only say to 'choose the follow-up route' based on the dashboard. Therefore, the condition that the workflow permits this for unresolved trends is not supported.",
        "status": "refuted"
      }
    },
    "r3": {
      "O": {
        "1": {
          "evidence": "The blue line starts at the 2010 tick aligned with the 2,000 y-axis tick and ends at the 2015 tick aligned with the 3,000 y-axis tick.",
          "status": "supported"
        },
        "2": {
          "evidence": "The x-axis is labeled 'Year' with ticks 2010-2015. The y-axis is labeled 'Population' with values increasing from 0 to 3,500.",
          "status": "supported"
        }
      },
      "B": {
        "reading_checked": "If the blue line is the dashboard's total-population series, the horizontal axis maps left-to-right positions to the printed years, and the vertical axis increases upward as labeled, then a line endpoint aligned with a higher y-axis tick at the later year represents population growth; if the routing workflow maps observed growth to growth planning, select the growth-planning route.",
        "evidence": "The form context explicitly states 'Population record: Total population', supporting the assumption that the line is the total population series. The axes are labeled and oriented as described (Year left-to-right, Population increasing upward). The line moves from a lower y-value (2,000) at an earlier year (2010) to a higher y-value (3,000) at a later year (2015), which represents population growth. The option 'Route to population growth planning' is available. The condition is met.",
        "status": "supported"
      }
    }
  }
